Describe the particle, fluid and frame of motion (@cm-particle-description: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-of-Aerosols-Ahmadi.lingua#r_175C6Q2GTKPZJJ6XSRHF5979G0", #source "../sources/Single-Particle-Transport-Kulkarni-Baron-Willeke.lingua#r_34AB62TA1PZDEMM8QQZ0W3A06B", #clean-manufacturing "../../../physics/fluid-dynamics/viscous/Creeping-flow-reversibility-and-a-translating-sphere.lingua#r_2NCJ64J8EHE6G7NWVKGK5DC3ZA") { r_5F3PY0RB5049PH41GMCBWCM5NE
**Read:** [The fluid mechanics of aerosols — Goodarz Ahmadi, Clarkson](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-of-Aerosols-Ahmadi.lingua#r_175C6Q2GTKPZJJ6XSRHF5979G0), hydrodynamic forces; [Fundamentals of single-particle transport — Kulkarni, Baron and Willeke](../sources/Single-Particle-Transport-Kulkarni-Baron-Willeke.lingua#r_34AB62TA1PZDEMM8QQZ0W3A06B), continuum and slip descriptions. Revisit [Continuum fields, molecular scales and relaxation](../../../physics/fluid-dynamics/foundations/Continuum-fields-molecular-scales-and-relaxation.lingua#r_52W3FJ90C69MPGFW3QNYXA6Q80).

Specify particle size, shape, density, composition and surface state, then fluid density, viscosity, temperature and motion. Define particle velocity v and local fluid velocity u in the same frame. Their difference drives drag; a fast laboratory-frame velocity does not imply large drag when the fluid moves with the particle.

The particle can be small relative to a room yet large relative to gas molecular scales, or small enough that those molecular scales matter. The room-scale Reynolds number and particle-scale Reynolds number answer different questions. A model that treats the fluid as continuous around a large object may still need a slip correction for a very small suspended particle.

**Work:** Draw both scales and define the length and velocity used in each ratio. Identify which properties are measured, inferred or hypothetical. Change the reference frame by a constant velocity and verify that the relative velocity and predicted drag remain unchanged.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
